# Probe 38 (scripts/probe_scatter_map_options.py): the labels and legend options scatter and map were never probed for, the two newest core types, which had none.
# Seen (bridge captures of both pages, then a real Home > Refresh + Ctrl+S): the legend object works on both types — 'Right' and 'Top' moved the legend and show = false left none, on the scatterChart and, the least sure prediction, on the map too. objects.labels did nothing visible on either type, and the save then settled it outright: Desktop DELETED the labels object from all four visuals carrying it, on the active scatter page and on the map page alike, while keeping every legend object exactly as written. Both types default to a legend at the BOTTOM and no labels, unlike pie and donut's right-hand legend in probe 37, so the default position is per type. The save also re-added "active": true to each scatter's X projection (probes 34, 36) and bumped $schema 2.13.0 -> 2.14.0 on the files it rewrote: all six on the active scatter page, but on the map page only the two it had to change, leaving the three map legend visuals untouched byte for byte. No auto filterConfig this time. The maps drew, so this install has "Map and filled map visuals" on. All content invented.

